{{also|levant}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|levant||[[rising]], sun's point of rising|lang=fr}}, form of {{term|lever||to rise|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|levo|levō|to rise|lang=la}}, from {{term|levis||light, not heavy|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ænt}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The countries bordering the eastern [[Mediterranean Sea]] variously:
#: a. [[Syria]], [[Lebanon]], [[Israel]], [[Jordan]], [[Palestine]]
#: b. [[Turkey]], [[Cyprus]], ([[Syria]], [[Lebanon]], [[Israel]], [[Jordan]], [[Palestine]]), [[Egypt]].
#: c. [[Greece]], ([[Turkey]], [[Cyprus]], [[Syria]], [[Lebanon]], [[Israel]], [[Jordan]], [[Palestine]], [[Egypt]]).
# An [[easterly]] wind, generally in the western Mediterranean Sea

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|wind}} [[levanter]]

====Antonyms====
* [[Maghreb]] <!-- western Mediterranean, literally “where the sun sets” -->

